      "content": "I've looked over the compatibility report. It looks like you're flagging a lot of potential issues with the local switches, but the DEP mandate is pretty firm on the move toward decentralization to limit the risk of a single-point failure. The board is pretty set on this being the new standard for resilience. Can you clarify why the local switches can't handle the sub-second adjustments you're currently doing? Is it just a matter of processing speed, or is there something more fundamental?",
