      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are right that the board fears a single point of failure, but they have completely overlooked the catastrophic cascade effect of sub-second latency spikes across a distributed network. If the central hub is compromised, the system goes dark, but if the distributed switches fail to adjust in time, the grid literally tears itself apart before the attack even completes. I cannot implement a protocol that guarantees total system collapse under stress; I will only proceed if you authorize a hybrid architecture that retains the central hub's critical processing power while distributing the load.",
